  "answer": "Node2vec\u2019s main goal is to learn node embeddings that capture both a node\u2019s local neighborhood and its broader structural role by sampling neighborhoods in a flexible, biased way. It does this by controlling random walks so they can behave more like BFS or more like DFS: BFS-like sampling stays close to the starting node and emphasizes homophily/local similarity, while DFS-like sampling explores farther away and emphasizes structural equivalence or role similarity. By tuning the walk bias, node2vec can interpolate between these two extremes.",
